#
# Counter-example for math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (Rule P3): a math:ProbabilityValue
# that names NEITHER its gmeow:hasReferenceFrame NOR its logic:probabilityModel, so the
# sh:or over those two arms fails — shacl.OrConstraintComponent (math:UnframedProbabilityValue).
# Single violation: its in-range math:quantityValue (0.5) keeps the range gate
# math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape (P1) SATISFIED, it is not typed math:OddsValue /
# math:LogOddsValue so math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape (P2) stays satisfied, and it
# carries no logic:confidence so math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint (P10) stays silent —
# EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling probability shape also fires.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityValue / math:UnframedProbabilityValue (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityValueUnframedBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:bareLiteralProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    math:quantityValue "0.5"^^xsd:decimal .
<http://example.org/math/bareLiteralProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
